2. DPF — ISC, fetched at build time
-----------------------------------

The DISTRHO Plugin Framework provides the plugin and UI scaffolding. It is
cloned into dpf/ by the build (see .devcontainer/scripts/20-dpf.sh) and is
deliberately NOT vendored here, so this repository contains none of its code.

    Copyright (C) 2012-2026 Filipe Coelho <falktx@falktx.com>
    ISC License — see dpf/LICENSE after cloning

DPF requires attribution regardless of the format built.


3. Plugin formats — per-format terms
------------------------------------

Each plugin API carries its own licence, which a built binary inherits. This
project builds CLAP and VST3 (src/Makefile: TARGETS = clap vst3):

    CLAP       MIT    Copyright 2014-2022 Alexandre Bique
    VST3       ISC    DPF's own "travesty" API definitions

Note on VST3: DPF does NOT use Steinberg's official VST3 SDK. Its API
definitions come from the travesty sub-project under DPF's own licence, which
is why building VST3 here carries no Steinberg licensing obligation.

The standalone/JACK target, used only for development, additionally pulls in
RtAudio and RtMidi (MIT, Copyright 2001-2021 Gary P. Scavone).

DPF can also target LADSPA and DSSI, whose headers are LGPLv2.1+. This project
does not build those, which is what keeps every shipped artifact free of
copyleft.

VST2 is deliberately not built: Steinberg revoked that SDK's licence, so new
development must not target it. See docs/spec.md section 2.


4. What the plugin reports to hosts
-----------------------------------

FortyFifthPlugin.cpp reports "MIT" through getLicense(), matching section 1.
An earlier version reported "ISC", which was DPF's licence rather than this
project's — the two are near-identical in effect, but the plugin should state
its own terms, not its framework's.


5. Music theory
---------------

The circle-of-fifths layout, chord spellings and scale-degree relationships
are music theory and are not copyrightable. Only a particular printed
product's artwork, palette and text are protected. Every visual element here
— palette, geometry, typography, proportions — is original to this project
and was not traced from any commercial chord wheel.


6. If you redistribute a built plugin
-------------------------------------

Include attribution for:

